  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.03377v1</id>
    <title>Amplifying Effective CXL Memory Bandwidth for LLM Inference via Transparent Near-Data Processing</title>
    <updated>2025-09-03T14:53:45Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.03377v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.03377v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Large language model (LLM) inference is bottlenecked by the limited bandwidth of CXL-based memory used for capacity expansion. We introduce CXL-NDP, a transparent near-data processing architecture that amplifies effective CXL bandwidth without requiring changes to the CXL.mem interface or AI models. CXL-NDP integrates a precision-scalable bit-plane layout for dynamic quantization with transparent lossless compression of weights and KV caches directly within the CXL device. In end-to-end serving, CXL-NDP improves throughput by 43%, extends the maximum context length by 87%, and reduces the KV cache footprint by 46.9% without accuracy loss. Hardware synthesis confirms its practicality with a modest silicon footprint, lowering the barrier for adopting efficient, scalable CXL-based memory in generative AI infrastructure.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-09-03T14:53:45Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.AR"/>
    <author>
      <name>Rui Xie</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Asad Ul Haq</name>
    </author>
